<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

{#- The site's second script, and the reason the menu never flashes open on load.
    It runs before the stylesheets are parsed, so by the time the header paints,
    base.css already knows JavaScript is available and has collapsed the nav.
    It must stay inline and stay here; an external file would arrive too late. -#}
<script>document.documentElement.className += " js";</script>

{#- The page's name, then the site's: "Fees · Sarah Philip". A search result shows the
    title with no surrounding context, so every page has to name the practice — "Fees"
    on its own identifies no business, no person and no country.

    site.name comes from src/_data/site.json, which Eleventy reads with no config of its
    own. The name is in a file rather than typed here because the briefing still lists
    the final site name as Sarah's to decide; when she does, it is one edit there.
    (header.njk and footer.njk still hold their own copies of the name — switching those
    over is a separate job, not this one.)

    metaTitle wins outright when a page sets one, for a page whose h1 does not work as a
    title. Only index.njk sets it, and Sarah never does: a post keeps the same three
    front matter fields it always had and picks up the suffix on its own. -#}
<title>{% if metaTitle %}{{ metaTitle }}{% else %}{{ title }} · {{ site.name }}{% endif %}</title>

{#- Wrapped, so a page with no description gets no tag rather than an empty one.
    Sarah publishes by editing front matter in GitHub's web editor; deleting the
    description line is a one-keystroke mistake, and content="" is a worse thing to
    ship than a missing tag — a search engine reads it as a description that is
    deliberately blank. -#}
{% if description %}<meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">{% endif %}

{#- fonts before tokens before base: @font-face, then the values, then the uses. -#}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/fonts.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/base.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/pages.css">
</head>
<body>

{% include "header.njk" %}

<main>{{ content | safe }}</main>

{% include "footer.njk" %}

{#- defer, so the header exists by the time it runs and menu.js needs no
    DOMContentLoaded wrapper. -#}
<script src="/scripts/menu.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
